WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.950
This guided practice applies the normalization
pattern to a different column The

00:00:04.975 --> 00:00:09.212
stored table should not be changed We only want a
display value

00:00:09.238 --> 00:00:14.962
in the query result Start by trimming
preferred_language Use

00:00:14.988 --> 00:00:19.462
NULLIF to convert an empty trimmed value to NULL
Then use COALESCE

00:00:19.488 --> 00:00:24.138
to replace the missing result with Language not
recorded The practice data

00:00:24.162 --> 00:00:28.612
includes one patient whose preferred language is
NULL Run the query and

00:00:28.638 --> 00:00:33.075
confirm that the stored column remains NULL while
the derived language_display column

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.412
shows the fallback label A SELECT expression can
standardize output without overwriting

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:39.112
source data
